/*! \page Solver_modes Solver modes and physics options

\section Solver_modes_modes Solver modes

| Mode | Description |
|---|---|
| full_system | CVODE on the full state vector, with a dense, banded, GMRES or KLU sparse-direct linear solver |
| active_window | two independent sliding windows, one over SIA size and one over vacancy size, with an OpenMP-parallel right-hand side |

In the active_window mode the number of threads is selected from the sweep length of the right-hand side, and it can be set with the environment variable OMP_NUM_THREADS. The same code path runs on one thread when OpenMP is not available.

\section Solver_modes_physics Physics options

The physics is selected by two independent choices.

| Choice | Values | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| equations | discrete or bin_moment | one ODE per size, or the logarithmic bin-moment grouping |
| cascade | fission or fusion | the cascade spectrum and the helium reduction |

The four combinations map to the strings that are used on disk:

| equations | cascade | physics_option |
|---|---|---|
| discrete | fission | full_CD_fission |
| discrete | fusion | full_CD_fusion |
| bin_moment | fission | bin_moment_CD_fission |
| bin_moment | fusion | bin_moment_CD_fusion |

The constructor of \ref py_utils::simulation::RadClusterSimulation "RadClusterSimulation" accepts either form. The functions make_physics_option() and split_physics_option() convert between them.

\section Solver_modes_linsol Linear solvers

| linsol | Linear solver |
|---|---|
| dense | dense direct |
| band | banded direct |
| gmres | GMRES, with the Jacobi or the Woodbury preconditioner |
| klu | KLU sparse direct, with a colored finite-difference Jacobian. Discrete equations only |

\section Solver_modes_domain Adaptive size domain

The method run_adaptive() of RadClusterSimulation expands the tracked cluster-size domain when the distribution reaches the top of the grid. The method run() integrates on a fixed domain.

\sa \ref Solver_preconditioner, \ref Core_reductions

*/
